{
  "title": "Align iOS cached title sort with server collation",
  "description": "The iOS recipe cache currently serves title-sorted browse \
results with `localizedCaseInsensitiveCompare`, while `GET /api/recipes` sorts \
by PostgreSQL `lower(title)` under the database collation. Accented and other \
non-ASCII titles can therefore appear in a different order when iOS switches \
between its cache and the server. Future local text search would inherit the \
same drift if it allowed title ordering.\n\
\n\
Choose one canonical title comparator that can run identically on the server \
and iOS, pin it with shared vectors covering case, accents, non-ASCII scripts, \
equal folded titles, and UUID tie-breaks, then update API and XCTest coverage. \
Until that contract lands, keep title-sorted text queries server-backed. Web \
continues to consume server order and needs no client comparator.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
    "search",
    "sorting",
    "parity",
  ],
